        "type": "uitleg",
        "tekst": "**From the lecture**\n\nThe lecture opens with exactly this move, with two questions on the slide: **why are you attending school today?** and **how can sociology help in making our society safer and more secure?** It then gives the same definition, with four phrases stacked on the slide: sociology as a **form of consciousness**, a **way of thinking**, a **critical way of seeing**, a **perspective**.\n\nThe lecturer's version of Berger uses the image of **seeing through, looking behind closed doors**, the **excitement** of the familiar turning into something with meaning, and **opening a gift with many layers**. The exam-relevant formulation on the slide is the one from the book: the first wisdom of sociology is that things are not what they seem."
